rompt": "_____________ explained that the sequence of drug use occurring starts with\nlegal drug and proceeds to illegal drugs.", "sourcePage": 5, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 547, "answer": {"text": "Gateway hypothesis", "source": {"id": "offline-c6580badb21d0062ed25", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 11.pdf", "sha256": "c6580badb21d0062ed25b7bd27a60d8f44b3527c985297dfd1d969c64e3e188e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/c6580badb21d0062ed25b7bd27a60d8f44b3527c985297dfd1d969c64e3e188e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/c6580badb21d0062ed25b7bd27a60d8f44b3527c985297dfd1d969c64e3e188e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}], "skills": ["reading"], "recordings": [], "answerSources": [{"id": "offline-c6580badb21d0062ed25", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 11.pdf", "sha256": "c6580badb21d0062ed25b7bd27a60d8f44b3527c985297dfd1d969c64e3e188e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/c6580badb21d0062ed25b7bd27a60d8f44b3527c985297dfd1d969c64e3e188e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/c6580badb21d0062ed25b7bd27a60d8f44b3527c985297dfd1d969c64e3e188e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}], "passages": []}, {"id": "dd7c0fa263be52af-p6", "label": "Part B · PART B", "part": "B", "sourceSha256": "dd7c0fa263be52afa81dcbd270165ac808203f14da1d95567b5d1af6ec63f130", "pages": [6, 7, 8, 9, 10, 11], "questions": [{"number": 1, "prompt": "Chronic urticaria;\nA Is caused by an allergic reaction to a food or drug.\nB Arises spontaneously and its cause is unknown.\nC Is a genetic disorder that is very rare.\nChronic urticaria\nChronic urticaria is a common condition characterized by recurrent hives lasting\nseveral weeks or months and is usually idiopathic. Approximately half of the\nindividuals with chronic urticaria will present with episodes of angioedema that\ncan be severe and debilitating. There is a 47-year-old Hispanic male who presented\ninitially for an evaluation of chronic hives following hospitalization due to hive-\ninduced anaphylaxis. The individual had a history significant for urticaria and\nangioedema beginning in his early 30s. Interestingly, both the individual’s 41-year-\nold sister and 12-year-old daughter were also affected by chronic urticaria and\nsevere angioedema. Whole exome sequencing of the proband and several family\nmembers revealed a heterozygous variant of uncertain significance in exon 2 of\nTNFAIP3, denoted as c.65G>A (p.R22Q), in all affected members.", "sourcePage": 6, "choices": ["A", "B", "C"], "kind": "question", "offset": 223, "answer": {"text": "B Arises spontaneously and its cause is unknown.", "source": {"id": "offline-c6580badb21d0062ed25", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 11.pdf", "sha256": "c6580badb21d0062ed25b7bd27a60d8f44b3527c985297dfd1d969c64e3e188e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/c6580badb21d0062ed25b7bd27a60d8f44b3527c985297dfd1d969c64e3e188e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/c6580badb21d0062ed25b7bd27a60d8f44b3527c985297dfd1d969c64e3e188e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 2, "prompt": "Arterial aneurysms;", "sourcePage": 6, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 1299, "answer": {"text": "A Are caused by narrowing of arteries.", "source": {"id": "offline-c6580badb21d0062ed25", "filename": "READING ANSWERS 11.pdf", "sha256": "c6580badb21d0062ed25b7bd27a60d8f44b3527c985297dfd1d969c64e3e188e", "assetPath": "https://github.com/genododi/OET/releases/download/genododi-library-2026-10-19-2/c6580badb21d0062ed25b7bd27a60d8f44b3527c985297dfd1d969c64e3e188e.pdf", "textPath": "imported-resources/text/c6580badb21d0062ed25b7bd27a60d8f44b3527c985297dfd1d969c64e3e188e.json", "format": "pdf", "role": "answer-key"}, "page": 1}}, {"number": 3, "prompt": "What is correct?", "sourcePage": 7, "choices": [], "kind": "question", "offset": 908, "answe